'''''Tripodion tetraphyllum''''' is a [[species]] of [[flowering plant]] in the [[legume]] family, [[Fabaceae]]. It is an annual herb, commonly known as '''annual kidney vetch''', native to the [[Mediterranean Basin]] of southern Europe, North Africa, and western Asia. It grows in the Mediterranean–[[Sahara]] transition zone of North Africa, and in anthropic landscapes.<ref name = powo/> It is the sole species in genus '''''Tripodion''''', which belongs to subfamily [[Faboideae]].<ref>{{Cite journal |last=Sokoloff |first=Dmitry |last2=Kramina |first2=Tatiana |date=2016-01-22 |title=The identity of Lotus antiochianus and taxonomic limits of Lotus and Hammatolobium (Leguminosae: Loteae) |url=https://biotaxa.org/Phytotaxa/article/view/phytotaxa.245.1.9 |journal=Phytotaxa |volume=245 |issue=1 |pages=75 |doi=10.11646/phytotaxa.245.1.9 |issn=1179-3163|url-access=subscription }}</ref>

The plants have a self-supporting growth form and compound, broad leaves. Individuals can grow to 0.2 m.<ref>{{Cite web|title=Tripodion tetraphyllum (L.)Fourr. - Encyclopedia of Life|url=https://eol.org/pages/689469|access-date=2022-02-04|website=eol.org}}</ref><ref>{{Cite web |last=Mifsud |first=Stephen |date=2002-08-23 |title=Tripodion tetraphyllum (Annual Kidney Vetch) : MaltaWildPlants.com - the online Flora of the Maltese Islands. |url=https://www.maltawildplants.com/FABC/Tripodion_tetraphyllum.php |access-date=2022-03-07 |website=www.maltawildplants.com |language=en-us}}</ref>

